//
// loft#1913, `@FR-Col-Spatial` / `@FR-Col-Axis` — a spatial axis is an integer-not-null
// coordinate.  A float or single axis was accepted, and the encoding then missed the
// collection's own records: `s[e.x, e.y]` answered null for every `e` the iteration yielded,
// and a float box query did not compile on `--native`.  Every non-integer scalar is refused at
// the declaration; integer axes of every width keep working (the `1431-…` and `col_spatial`
// cells).
//
// @falsified-at: 27e83e117 — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/3 -> 0/3 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/3 -> 0/3 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
// @falsified-by: tests/falsified/1913-a-spatial-axis-is-an-integer.patch — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/3 -> 0/3 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/3 -> 0/3 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
//   CHANNEL: the EXPECTATION — the control accepts all three axes.
//   HOLDS: leak, panic, free-refusal and the other cells are equal on BOTH trees, and
